puddle doctor (puddle 0.1.0, linux x86_64)

ok    CPU virtualization  on (the hypervisor uses it)
ok    Hypervisor          /dev/kvm is usable
ok    Bundled runtime     msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (/opt/puddle/runtime/msb)
ok    Runtime starts      msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (0.0 s)
ok    Test boot           a test VM booted and ran a program in 1.1 s
ok    Disk space          120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
FAIL  Data folder path    /srv/team belongs to another user (id 1001); /srv/team is writable by the group and not sticky, so msb will not open Puddle's data below them
      fix:  msb trusts only folders you or root own. If /srv/team is yours, run `sudo chown
            "$USER" /srv/team`; otherwise point XDG_DATA_HOME at a folder you own.
            msb opens its catalog only below folders where other accounts cannot rename entries,
            so every sandbox start fails until the write permission is gone. A user created with
            a private group and umask 0002 (the Ubuntu default) often leaves ~/.local at 0775.
            Run:
              sudo chmod g-w /srv/team
      from: /srv/team owner id 1001
            /srv/team mode 0775
ok    Disk encryption     data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked

1 problem to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

